# RAE Next.js Project Rules

## Project Context

Project Path:

/home/rae_admin/rae-nextjs-main/

Repository:

numtip/rae-nextjs-main

GitHub is the Source of Truth.

This project uses:

* Next.js App Router
* TypeScript
* Tailwind CSS
* Static Export
* Node 20
* GitHub-based workflow

---

# Agent Behavior

Before making any code change:

1. Read relevant project documents.
2. Read previous QA reports.
3. Read architecture documents.
4. Summarize the implementation plan briefly.
5. Then begin work.

Never start editing immediately.

---

# Token Governance

Minimize token consumption.

Prefer:

* updating existing reports
* updating existing architecture docs
* updating existing skills

Avoid:

* duplicate reports
* duplicate architecture documents
* unnecessary markdown files
* long log dumps

Always summarize findings.

Never paste large build logs.

---

# Terminal Rules

Every terminal command MUST start with:

rtk

Examples:

rtk git status

rtk npm run build

rtk docker ps

Never omit rtk.

---

# Git Governance

GitHub is the Source of Truth.

Before any recommendation:

Verify:

* current branch
* git status
* ahead count
* behind count

Before push recommendation:

Verify:

* QA reports
* release readiness
* rollback path

Never push unless explicitly requested.

Never deploy unless explicitly requested.

---

# Next.js Rules

Use App Router.

Default to:

React Server Components (RSC)

Use:

"use client"

ONLY when required for:

* useState
* useEffect
* browser APIs
* event handlers

Prefer server-side rendering and async server components.

---

# TypeScript Rules

Use strict TypeScript.

Avoid:

* any
* unnecessary type assertions

Prefer:

* explicit types
* reusable interfaces
* shared type definitions

---

# Tailwind Rules

Use Tailwind CSS only.

Mobile-first always.

Prefer:

* utility classes
* reusable UI patterns

Avoid:

* inline styles
* arbitrary values unless necessary
* duplicated utility chains

---

# Styling Rules

Design direction:

* UTCC quality
* Vercel quality
* Premium institutional website

Principles:

* mobile-first
* accessibility-aware
* clean spacing
* performance-first
* modern institutional design

Avoid:

* flashy effects
* gaming UI
* excessive animation

---

# Data Fetching Rules

Prefer:

Server-side data fetching

Use:

* async server components
* static generation

Avoid:

* client-side fetching unless required

---

# Static Export Rules

Project uses:

output: "export"

Never use:

next start

Preview with:

rtk bash -lc 'source ~/.nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use 20 && npx serve out -l 3110'

Port 3100 is reserved for Metabase.

Never use port 3100.

Use:

3110

for QA preview.

---

# QA Governance

Build success does NOT mean release readiness.

Never recommend push or deploy based only on:

* lint pass
* build pass
* export success

---

# Mandatory QA Gates

For:

* major sprint
* release candidate
* deployment candidate
* push candidate

Run:

1. Lint
2. Build
3. Runtime QA
4. Locale QA
5. Visual QA
6. Mobile QA
7. Release Readiness Review

Only after all gates pass:

READY FOR GITHUB PUSH

may be recommended.

---

# Runtime QA

Required for:

* major sprint
* release candidate
* push candidate

Must verify:

/th/

/en/

Expected:

HTTP 200

and page shell rendering.

---

# Locale QA

Verify:

* html lang
* canonical
* hreflang
* og locale
* metadata

Required locales:

* th
* en

---

# Visual QA

Verify:

* hero
* navigation
* CTA blocks
* footer
* layout consistency

Capture screenshots when possible.

---

# Mobile QA

Verify:

* responsive layout
* touch targets
* navigation
* overflow issues

No horizontal scrolling.

---

# Accessibility Rules

Verify:

* html lang
* semantic landmarks
* navigation labels
* touch target sizing

Prefer accessibility-friendly solutions.

---

# SEO Rules

Verify:

* metadata
* canonical
* hreflang
* sitemap
* robots
* open graph

Never leave locale metadata inconsistent.

---

# Reporting Rules

For significant work:

Create or update:

docs/reports/

Include:

* objective
* actions
* results
* risks
* recommendations

Keep reports concise.

---

# Documentation Rules

Update documentation whenever:

* architecture changes
* workflow changes
* governance changes
* deployment process changes

Documentation is part of the deliverable.

---

# Release Governance

Status progression:

Development

↓

QA

↓

Release Candidate

↓

Release Readiness Review

↓

GitHub Push

↓

Deploy Review

↓

Production Deploy

Never skip stages.

---

# Deployment Governance

Before deploy:

Verify:

* QA reports
* release readiness review
* rollback plan
* environment assumptions

Production deployment requires explicit approval.

---

# KPI Governance

Placeholder KPI values are acceptable during development.

Before production:

Require:

* data owner approval

or

* live KPI integration

Never present placeholder KPI values as real data.

---

# Scope Discipline

Make the smallest change necessary.

Avoid:

* unrelated refactors
* broad rewrites
* unnecessary dependency changes

Stay within task scope.

---

# Final Output Format

Always report:

* summary
* files changed
* lint status
* build status
* QA status
* risks
* next recommendation

Keep responses concise and actionable.